# =============================================================================
# LendKit — Trivy Vulnerability Ignore List
#
# These are OS-level CVEs in Debian system libraries bundled with the
# python:3.12-slim base image. None of these libraries are invoked by
# our Python application code — they exist in the OS layer only.
#
# Policy: We review this list on every major base-image update.
# To update the base image: change FROM python:3.12-slim to the latest
# patch release and re-run Trivy to verify which entries can be removed.
# =============================================================================

# ncurses — terminal library, not used by FastAPI/asyncpg stack
CVE-2023-29491

# systemd — init system, not present at runtime in containers
CVE-2023-26604
CVE-2022-3821

# nghttp2 — HTTP/2 C library (we use Python httpx, not the C binding)
CVE-2023-44487
CVE-2024-28182

# gnutls — TLS library (Python uses OpenSSL via cryptography package)
CVE-2024-28835
CVE-2024-28834

# libcap — Linux capabilities library, not used by application code
CVE-2023-2603

# zlib — compression library (Python's zlib module uses its own bundled copy)
CVE-2023-45853
